From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chelovechishee <261262090+chelovechishee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 35/46] arm64: dts: gta3xlwifi: S2MU005 wakes the system on a
 cable change

The charger sets the input current from the BC1.2 result when VBUS comes
or goes, but asleep its interrupt is disabled: a cable plugged in during
s2idle charged at the bootloader's 500 mA until something else woke the
tablet. Mark the PMIC as a wakeup source; the I2C core then makes its
interrupt a wake IRQ and sec-common keeps it armed over suspend.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts
index c94c9f9bb..1a98cf704 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts
@@ -382,6 +382,11 @@ pmic@3d {
 		interrupt-parent = <&gpa2>;
 		interrupts = <2 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		monitored-battery = <&battery>;
+		/*
+		 * A cable plugged in or out during sleep wakes the tablet, so the
+		 * charger sets the input current for it; asleep it stays at 500 mA.
+		 */
+		wakeup-source;
 	};
 };
 
